==English==

===Etymology===
# Short for [[shove it up your ass|Shove it up your ass!]].
===Interjection===
{{en-interj|head=[[up|Up]] [[yours|yours!]]}}

# {{context|idiomatic|offensive|markedly|vulgar|lang=en}} Expression to show discontent with the other party, or to show contempt.
#: ''You dare come here dressed so horribly? Well, '''up yours!'''
# {{context|idiomatic|dismissive|offensive|markedly|vulgar|lang=en}} Go away! Go to hell!
#: '''''Up yours!'''—I’m not giving you any!''
#: ''You’ve done enough to ruin our outing, so '''up yours!'''

